olution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =0[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068029/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e3191812156f778cf041de5e56cf3304a8e6b4429721951f136737307b01287"} {"question" "q-334058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb604fd16125fd3998071ecdad93c8fe8f058039da92f0ee65999b5bfaf0e16f"} {"question" "q-334058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/d