e5e56cf3304a8e6b4429721951f136737307b01287"} {"question" "q-334132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=6+3\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=6+3\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(6+3\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(6+3\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+3\\text{i}{e}^{6t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3{e}^{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {e}^{6t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))+\\text{i}{e}^{6t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\ {e}^{6t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068029/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e3191812156f778cf041de5e56cf3304a8e6b4429721951f136737307b01287"} {"question" "q-334132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bb604fd16125fd3998071ecdad93c8fe8f058039da92f0ee65999b5bfaf0e16f"} {"question" "q-334132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068029/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e3191812156f778cf041de5e56cf3304a8e6b4429721951f136737307b01287"} {"question" "q-334132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/